 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? That's usually the bottom bracket bearings or the frame rubbing on the drive side. Which does your bike do? Please don't. Cooking oil is sticky for a bit, then gets gummy, and can cause even more damage. Carefully lift the bottom bracket out of its cup, and then brush any dirt out. Put fresh grease in with a greasy lint free cloth. Clean it only if it' really dirty. Most bike shops have a dedicated bike cleaner.",
